# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. Checked out with CRLF - which happens on
# Windows with core.autocrlf on - a script fails as `bad interpreter`, which
# reads like a missing shell rather than a line ending. setup-linux.sh and
# setup-mac.sh are files people download and run, so this is worth pinning
# rather than relying on every contributor's git configuration.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Translation catalogs, for the same reason one level up: they are edited by
# Weblate, by Poedit and by hand on three platforms, and a file that changes
# every line each time it crosses one makes a diff unreadable and a merge
# conflict out of nothing. polib reads CRLF perfectly well - that was measured,
# not assumed - so this is about the tools around it rather than about us.
*.po text eol=lf
*.pot text eol=lf
